# Round-8 MINOR 2. The four files below were EOL-converted on a Windows checkout
# while the briefs and content files held their bytes: `git -c core.autocrlf=true
# clone --no-local` of this branch produced a `key.json` with 1443 CR characters
# and 0 in the briefs. Nothing broke — JSON.parse is EOL-agnostic and
# `git hash-object` applies the clean filter, so sanitizeClone()'s key-blob
# assertion still computed the right sha — but re-running assemble-key.js on
# such a checkout rewrote key.json wholesale and showed a 1400-line diff that
# was pure line endings. A sealed corpus has to be byte-identical everywhere.
key.json -text
base-pool.json -text
construction-notes.json -text
materialized.json -text
blind-read.json -text
blind-draw-round*.json -text
